<div class="mw-parser-output"><h1>Use</h1>
<p>Usage:
</p>
<pre>use &lt;staff&gt;
use &lt;wand&gt; &lt;target&gt;
</pre>
<p>Examples:
</p>
<pre>hold wand
use wand rat
</pre>
<p>Staves and wands are a way to carry magic with you. A staff affects everyone 
where you are except you and your group; a wand must be used at a single 
target, and not while you are blind. Other players are touched by them 
only when both of you have signed the Book of Blood. To use one you must hold 
it in your hand (see <a cmd='#'>Help Hold</a>), and you must have practiced the skill wand 
use: how well it works depends on that skill and your brain against the power 
of the magic in it.
</p><p>The skill wand use is taught by the conjurers and sorcerers from guild 
level 0, the necromancers from level 1 (up to 80%) and the druids from 
level 8. Gustav, in the back room of the inn in Udgaard, 
teaches it to anyone up to 35%. Practising it needs brain 20.
</p><p>Each use takes a charge, even when nothing happens, and a bad failure 
drains a second one. Each staff and wand holds only so many charges. When they are used up, it is 
"drained of all power" until it is charged again (see <a cmd='#'>Help Charge Wand</a> and 
<a cmd='#'>Help Charge Staff</a>).
</p><p><br />
See Also:
</p>
<pre>&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Hold</a>
&gt; <a cmd='#'>Help Practice</a>
</pre>




</div>